---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
import Heading from "../components/Heading.astro";
import Prose from "../components/Prose.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Pavel Savinov - senior backend engineer (Go) based in Belgrade. Four years of production Go at Avito, Aviasales and Uzum."
>
  <section class="about">
    <Heading as="h1">About</Heading>
    <Prose>
      <p>
        I'm Pavel Savinov, a senior backend engineer working in Go. I have four years of
        production Go on high-volume distributed systems at Avito, Aviasales and Uzum:
        classifieds, flight search and e-commerce logistics with 15-50M monthly users. I'm based
        in Belgrade (CET) and open to remote roles, B2B contracts and relocation to the
        Netherlands or Germany.
      </p>

      <h2>Highlights</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Cut search API p99.9 latency from ~5 s to ~500 ms at Aviasales through pprof-driven
          optimization, caching and request shaping.
        </li>
        <li>
          Took a parcel-sorting system at Uzum from PRD to production in 4 months: domain and
          PostgreSQL model, Kafka integration via transactional outbox.
        </li>
        <li>
          Kept 20+ promotion microservices at 99.9%+ availability (~3.5k RPS) at Avito.
        </li>
        <li>
          Moved badge logic from mobile and web clients to a config-driven backend: a rollout went
          from a sprint plus app releases to a 30-minute config change.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Stack</h2>
      <p>
        Go, PostgreSQL, Kafka, Redis, gRPC, Kubernetes, Prometheus, Grafana, Jaeger. I use Claude
        Code and custom agent harnesses in daily work.
      </p>

      <h2>Selected public work</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <a href="https://github.com/getjump/pr-review">pr-review</a> - an agent skill that
          reviews a pull request by running it: three builds, one subtraction, then probes for
          what no test covers.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://github.com/getjump/protondb-game-compatibility-prediction"
            >protondb-game-compatibility-prediction</a
          > - predicting Linux game compatibility from 350K+ community reports with a two-stage
          LightGBM cascade, 0.871 F1.
          <a href="/posts/01-protondb-compatibility-ml-x-claude">Write-up</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://github.com/getjump/ru-php-the-right-way">ru-php-the-right-way</a> -
          Russian translation of PHP: The Right Way, maintained by the community.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Writing</h2>
      <p>
        Distributed systems, testing and building software with AI agents. Recent posts include
        <a href="/posts/01-protondb-compatibility-ml-x-claude">I Don't Know ML. Claude Does.</a>
        and
        <a href="/posts/02-detector-before-protocol">I Built the Detector Before the Protocol. Then Two Agents Fought Over It.</a>
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/getjump">LinkedIn</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/getjump">GitHub</a></li>
        <li><a href="mailto:getjump0@gmail.com">getjump0@gmail.com</a></li>
      </ul>
    </Prose>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about {
    max-width: var(--width-content);
  }
</style>
